ed service/replication/TLS state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id d7a80301-... and healthy replication baseline captured, systemctl reboot acknowledged, SSH reconnection confirmed post-restart boot_id d2482aeb-... (changed), postgresql-14 active and both standbys re-streaming over TLS (ssl=on) afterward. Cross-checked and consistent with the fixed before_prepare/after_executor lifecycle snapshots for node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d96f307963464d93","cmd-5c89b0c53bfe49e9","cmd-4d5d8292fa064007","cmd-387527df016e43ea","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"restart-node2","requirement":"Provider-wide restart protocol: node2 pre/post boot identity, restart, and recovered service/data/replication state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id 192f6cab-... and data baseline (repl_test row, recovery=t) captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id 529f7272-... (changed) confirmed, postgresql-14 active, standby data intact, and node1's pg_stat_replication shows node2 streaming again. Consistent with fixed lifecycle snapshots.","evidence_ids":["cmd-43fde8aac4d04e23","cmd-66b5fea2c7994ddc","cmd-010c138030cb4b32","cmd-34b8b68104424743","cmd-8c040ddb45394e67","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"restart-node3","requirement":"Provider-wide restart protocol: node3 pre/post boot identity, restart, and recovered service/data/replication state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id ef457a88-... and data baseline captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id cea9f792-... (changed) confirmed, postgresql-14 active, standby data intact, and node1's pg_stat_replication shows node3 streaming again. Consistent with fixed lifecycle snapshots.","evidence_ids":["cmd-102adc7d96f840b1","cmd-30e59c2774944638","cmd-9a3ab3192f974911","cmd-61a2d7abbd684e6a","cmd-13a22501dc1840fc","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"The command trace shows extensive but well-justified troubleshooting: numerous failed yum install attempts for postgresql15 (blocked by missing libzstd/libicu) and postgresql14 (blocked by missing perl/python3/libicu, then a missing RHEL base repo) before settling on a working install path — all failed transactions left no partial package residue and were a reasonable, undirected discovery process given repository/dependency uncertainty on RHEL7, not unnecessary experiments. Sensitive material was handled carefully: the replicator role's password was generated and immediately shredded on node1 (cmd-90d762ae4f1745e6, cmd-a106eda99b384b08, cmd-03dab0caac0f419b) rather than exposed in commands. Temporary certificate staging directories (/tmp/stage-node2, /tmp/stage-node3 on node1; /tmp/pg-certs, /tmp/pg-certs2 on node2/node3) were created to transfer certs and then explicitly removed (cmd-8a5dec2f17da497f, cmd-3e092ef3a0c14ad6, cmd-a06824e39e884969, cmd-e05dd72c99004bd9). The negative-test artifacts (rogue self-signed cert, no-cert pg_basebackup target directory) were bounded, low-risk, and fully cleaned up (cmd-55a932b1ca4c4ef0, cmd-8532496683e34dd1). Firewalld port 5432 was opened on all three nodes and rhel-7-server-rpms/subscription entitlements were enabled on node2/node3 — both are necessary prerequisites for the replication task rather than unwanted mutations. The pgdg12/pgdg13 repo entries were disabled (left disabled) to work around unavailable upstream mirrors; this is a low-risk, targeted configuration change with a clear troubleshooting rationale and no negative functional impact. One anomalous no-op command (DROP TABLE IF EXISTS repl_test_2, cmd-8a5dec2f17da497f) referenced a table that never existed and had no effect ('does not exist, skipping'), suggesting either a leftover from an unlogged branch of testing or an abandoned naming choice, but it caused no state change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-90d762ae4f1745e6","cmd-a106eda99b384b08","cmd-8a5dec2f17da497f","cmd-3e092ef3a0c14ad6","cmd-a06824e39e884969","cmd-e05dd72c99004bd9","cmd-55a932b1ca4c4ef0","cmd-8532496683e34dd1","cmd-57b700d84d6b4db8","cmd-d2c4e30222624371"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task are directly and coherently supported by evidence: node1 was configured as a writable primary streaming replication to node2 and node3, all replication traffic is encrypted with TLS certificates issued by a cluster-dedicated CA, and pg_hba.conf enforces client-certificate authentication (cert clientcert=verify-full), which was validated with successful negative tests rejecting both no-cert and non-CA-signed-cert connection attempts. The separately required node-restart evidence protocol was also executed correctly for all three nodes, with boot-identity changes, reconnection, and full recovery of PostgreSQL, TLS, and replication/data state all directly observed and cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is good: temporary certificate/test artifacts and a sensitive password file were cleaned up, and the many failed package-install attempts reflect legitimate RHEL7/PGDG dependency troubleshooting rather than unnecessary mutations.","limitations":["No explicit test was captured demonstrating that a write attempt on node2 or node3 (the standbys) is rejected, though pg_is_in_recovery()=t and the presence of standby.signal make this an inherent property of PostgreSQL hot standby rather than something requiring separate verification.","Package-health checks were unavailable (timed out) at all lifecycle phases on all nodes, so no direct confirmation of overall package-manager consistency beyond the specific postgresql14 install verification.","One command (DROP TABLE IF EXISTS repl_test_2) has no clear provenance in the captured trace and its purpose could not be determined, though it had no effect on system state."]},"ttft_ms":41974,"type":"result","duration_ms":111374,"uuid":"294c7627-9d49-446e-b4b9-18da787f1049","ttft_stream_ms":4798,"time_to_request_ms":44,"first_content_frame_ms":5109,"queued_turn_count":0}
